Prim's Algorithm – Conclusion, Time Complexity & Space Complexity
1. Conclusion:

Thus, Prim's Algorithm is used to find the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) of a connected weighted graph. 
  It selects the minimum-weight edge at each step without forming a cycle and calculates the minimum total cost.
This program helps us connect all vertices with minimum cost.

2. Time Complexity:

O(n²)

Because the program uses nested loops to find the minimum-weight edge in the graph.

3. Space Complexity:

O(n²)

Because the program uses an adjacency matrix of size n × n to store the graph.
